sprite sessions - Manage running exec sessions

Why Sessions?
  When you run a command with `sprite exec`, it becomes a session you can
  monitor, reattach to, or kill later.

  TTY sessions (interactive shells) keep running after detach. Non-TTY sessions
  suspend on detach to preserve output — they resume when you reattach.

  Active sessions keep your sprite alive — it won't pause while a TTY session
  is generating output.

Usage:
  sprite sessions <subcommand>

Subcommands:
  list, ls     List running sessions
  attach <id>  Attach to a session
  kill <id>    Kill a session

Options:
  -o, --org <name>       Specify organization
  -s, --sprite <name>    Specify sprite
  -h, --help             Show this help message

Examples:
  sprite sessions list               # List running sessions
  sprite s ls                        # Short form
  sprite sessions attach 12345       # Attach to session 12345
  sprite sessions kill 12345         # Kill session 12345
  sprite sessions kill 12345 --signal INT --timeout 5s

Common Workflow:
  # Start a dev server (detach with Ctrl+\)
  sprite exec -tty npm run dev

  # Check what's running
  sprite sessions list

  # Reattach to see its output
  sprite sessions attach 12345

  # Detach again with Ctrl+\

  # Done with it
  sprite sessions kill 12345

When to Use:
  - `sprite sessions attach <id>` — reattach by numeric session ID
  - `sprite attach <command>` — smart match by command name (e.g., `sprite attach bash`)
  - `sprite console` — start a new interactive shell session

Related Commands:
  sprite exec --help        Run commands
  sprite attach --help      Smart-attach by session ID or command name
  sprite console --help     Open a new interactive shell
